! AlwaysOn: EnergyPlus needs a schedule where the xlsx gives none: for loads whose schedule in the prototype is constant 1, and for the operating mode of the heat pump fans (the xlsx dictionary says constant volume fan control: the fan runs continuously).
  Schedule:Compact,
    AlwaysOn,                     !- Name
    ,                             !- Schedule Type Limits Name
    Through: 12/31,               !- Field 1
    For: AllDays,                 !- Field 2
    Until: 24:00,                 !- Field 3
    1;                            !- Field 4

! AlwaysOff: EnergyPlus needs a schedule for people, lights and equipment; the xlsx has no schedule for these loads and the schedule of the prototype is not constant 1 (zero load).
  Schedule:Compact,
    AlwaysOff,                    !- Name
    ,                             !- Schedule Type Limits Name
    Through: 12/31,               !- Field 1
    For: AllDays,                 !- Field 2
    Until: 24:00,                 !- Field 3
    0;                            !- Field 4

  Schedule:Compact,
    ACTIVITY_SCH,                 !- Name  Source: NREL PDF Table B-4, p.78 (page 89 of the file): ACTIVITY_SCH, All, 120 for all 24 hours.
    ,                             !- Schedule Type Limits Name
    Through: 12/31,               !- Field 1
    For: AllDays,                 !- Field 2
    Until: 24:00,120.;            !- Field 3

! HVAC system type of every zone from the xlsx (Zone and HVAC System Summary, HVAC System Type Dictionary): 7 VAV with reheat (chilled water cooling, hot-water fossil fuel boiler) for the core and perimeter zones, 12 SZ-CV-HW (single-zone constant volume, chilled water cooling, hot-water boiler heating) for the basement, 14 WSHP (CRAC) (water source heat pump, fluid cooler, hot-water fossil fuel boiler) for the data centers; the plenums have none (NA). The xlsx names the HVAC system of each zone (raw_data column I). All equipment data are EnergyPlus defaults.
! One thermostat for all zones: the xlsx gives the set point schedules for the office zones and says that the basement and the data centers are excepted (sheet Schedule Summary), but the template needs a thermostat for every zone, so those zones use the office set points too.
  HVACTemplate:Thermostat,
    OfficeThermostat,             !- Name
    HTGSETP_SCH_YES_OPTIMUM,      !- Heating Setpoint Schedule Name  Source: xlsx Schedule Summary 'Heating Set Point', rows 77/78/79 (Mon - Fri/Sat/Sun).
    ,                             !- Constant Heating Setpoint
    CLGSETP_SCH_NO_SETBACK;       !- Cooling Setpoint Schedule Name  Source: xlsx Schedule Summary 'Cooling Set Point', rows 74/75/76 (Mon - Fri/Sat/Sun).

